  "answer": "On this worktree the research pipeline's owner-facing decision points are the agentspec HumanCheckpoint plus the source_policy / owner_tor_flag gate and catalog owner_approval_required units. Of 8 candidate checkpoints, 4 retain positive EVPI (subsequent plans diverge) and 3 are eliminated as zero-EVPI permission theatre \u2014 progress acknowledgement, schema-looks-ok, and continue-versus-proceed all map both answers onto the same plan. OQ-3 already binds release mode to PR-ONLY, so re-asking it is eliminated as already-settled even though the counterfactual plans diverge. The minimal set, asked one foundational question at a time with the stated default, is: (1) public-tor opt-in, default keep-unavailable / fail closed; (2) unbounded paid spend, default keep-hard-cap; (3) ship controversial-lineage claims, default withhold, asked only if tor_stage is on because collection is not emission; (4) owner-blocked escalation, default fail-closed. SUCCESS:RES-0172",
